    "title": "Hackathon Travel Funds - Resources for All | University of Cincinnati",
    "text": "Hackathon Travel Funds - Resources for All | University of Cincinnati\n\nSkip to main content\n\n# Hackathon Travel Funds\n\nThe University of Cincinnati's Center for Entrepreneurship is now providing financial support to CEAS students wishing to travel in order to compete in Hackathons.\n\nThese payments will be paid as catalyst disbursements. Whether financial support, prize, or award, payment is defined as a scholarship and educational resource. Payment could adjust or limit federal aid eligibility.\n\nThis form is to have travel costs up to $500 per group can be reimbursed—no amount above $500 can be given at this time.\n\nThese funds are to cover your travel expenses, i.e. gas costs or airfare, to and from a Hackathon event.\n\nTRAVEL VIA CAR:\n\nThe center will reimburse $0.625/mile traveled as per university recommendations.\n\nSo, for example, if you are traveling via car 300 miles to a Chicago Hackathon, we will reimburse:\n\n300 (miles) x $0.625/mile = $187.50\n\nTRAVEL VIA AIRFARE:\n\nFor this application, we will reimburse flight costs up to $500 per group (not $500 each). If you plan to travel to the hackathon via air, please upload a photo of the flight you plan to purchase below.\n\nAFTER HACKATHON COMPETITION\n\nFor proof of attendance at the hackathon/competition, you will need to submit either:\n\nA link to your Devpost.com project from the hackathon/competition.\n\nOR IF YOU DON'T HAVE ONE\n\nWe will ask hackathon organizers for confirmation of your attendance.\n\nTWO STEPS TO APPLY:\n\nSCHOLAR"
