    "text": "e-Fest® 2026 - e-Fest | Undergraduate Entrepreneurship Competition\n\nHome Of The Schulze Entrepreneurship Challenge\n\nMore than a competition.\n\nCompete for $250,000 in cash prizes and join the Top 25 undergraduate startup teams from across North America.\n\nSubmit Your Pitch\n\n### Considering applying to e-Fest 2026? Here’s how to get started:\n\n1\n\nDecide to go for it!\n\n1. Commit to competing.Take your venture to the next level by applying to be part of the 10th anniversary of e-Fest—the ultimate capstone experience for undergraduate entrepreneurs.\n\n2\n\nCreate your pitch deck & video!\n\n2. Build your pitch.Start crafting your pitch deck and video now. Explore our Download Library for expert resources, templates, and inspiration to help your ideas shine.\n\n3\n\nSubmit your pitch to e-Fest 2026!\n\n3. Mark your calendar.Save the date and be ready when submissions open on January 7, 2026. This is your chance to showcase your venture on a national stage.\n\nReady to Submit? Get Started Here\n\n### $250K in cash prizes\n\nTake home a portion of $250K in cash prizes across four competitions to help launch your business.\n\n### Development awards\n\nReceive $2,500 to support entrepreneurship related programs and activities at your school.\n\n### Travel stipends\n\nUp to $3,750 in travel stipends offered for airfare, hotel and meals during the event in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n\n### Networking\n\nNetwork with other top student entrepreneurs and industry professionals from across the nation.\n\n### Learn from leaders"
